# Music and media

Play audio from your device or from **Dropbox**, log **how music makes you feel**, and let Help pick tracks by mood.

## Play music

- **Help:** *“play Pink Floyd”*, *“play something that will make me feel upbeat”*, or *“download and play Submergence”* (remote file on Dropbox).
- **Remote download + play:** Help topic **download music from remote filesystem and play it directly** walks you through the Dropbox picker, download, and in-app player.
- **Collection:** organize artists under **me → my things → music** (see **add a song to my music** in Help).

![Help matches a download-and-play question](<asset://images/help_music_search_partial_matches_cyber.png>)

![Playback from the in-app music service](<asset://images/help_music_playback_notification.png>)

Android may ask to read **Music and audio** before playback. Link [cloud provider setup](noetic://document/cloud%20provider%20setup) first for remote files.

## Emotion log

Under **me → my things → emotions**, keep feeling names you use (*upbeat*, *focused*, *calm*). Tell Help: *“I felt happy listening to …”* so mood-based playback improves over time.

## Video demos

Bundled tutorial clips (when present) play via automation in **Show me** scripts—not required for daily use.

